  "cause": "A large consuming recvmsg merges preceding ordinary bytes and a descriptor-bearing sendmsg. Its returned bytes/cmsg/length omit the descriptor-bearing skb start, so an end marker cannot preserve C per-frame prefix semantics.",
  "normal_client_scope": "Pinned libubus sends one header+blob per writev_retry; ordinary separate sendmsg controls pass. Custom callers batching frames or attaching descriptors during body reception demonstrate the mismatch.",
  "decision": "Correctness before performance: retire cross-frame consuming read-ahead. Use prefix-bounded recvmsg and frame-bounded read, retain shared stack and exact residual ownership as independent storage choices.",
  "references": [
    "https://github.com/gregkh/linux/blob/v6.12.94/net/unix/af_unix.c",
    "https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/unix.7.html",
    "https://github.com/gregkh/linux/blob/v6.12.94/net/core/scm.c",
    "https://github.com/gregkh/linux/blob/v6.12.94/include/net/scm.h"
  ]
